Implemented in [frontend/index.php](frontend/index.php). The petals use the same technique as the chickens: hand-authored SVG in the HTML, with JavaScript rewriting each `transform` every frame — no CSS animation for the petals, no generated markup.

**What changed**
- **14 sunflower petals** ([index.php:4687](frontend/index.php#L4687)) around the existing flower head, in two alternating golds (`#f4d772` / `#e5bb4f`) with a faint crease. Their bases tuck behind the head disc, and their authored rotations mean the flower is complete without JavaScript. Tip radii measure a uniform 27.9 px on screen, so the ring is even.
- **One hidden flight petal** ([index.php:4703](frontend/index.php#L4703)), always the departing petal, so only one can ever be airborne.
- **Petal script** ([index.php:6944](frontend/index.php#L6944)), directly after the chicken script and built the same way: IIFE, per-element state seeded from `data-a`, `draw()` writing transforms, `dt` clamped to 50 ms, `IntersectionObserver` pause, and an early return for `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- One CSS rule gives the petals `pointer-events: none` ([index.php:1974](frontend/index.php#L1974)).

**Behaviour**
- Each petal breathes with two summed low-frequency sines, ±0.45–0.9°, unique phase — layered on the stem's existing sway, effectively imperceptible.
- First departure 4–7 s after the hero becomes visible, then a random 6–12 s after each flight ends.
- A random petal is picked; the mode is a coin flip between **upward** (9–11 s, slow rise, lateral flutter, tumble) and **horizontal** (7–9 s, left or right at random, gentle bow, tumble). Both fade before leaving the scene.
- 450 ms after detachment, the empty slot grows a fresh petal in 520 ms with a slight elastic overshoot, while the loose one is still drifting.

**Verification**
- `php -l` clean; `git diff --check` clean; 172 insertions in one file.
- Page serves HTTP 200 with all 14 petals.
- Live sampling observed a horizontal right-hand pass, a vertical rise, and a clean launch where exactly one resident slot was empty and one replacement was growing; the flight node was the only one visible at a time.
- No console messages or errors.
- The reduced-motion and JS-off paths are implemented and the static markup is complete, but I did not emulate the reduced-motion media query in the browser.

The mockup [altaslife-chicken-roaming.html](frontend/altaslife-chicken-roaming.html) and the chicken script are untouched.

The departures are deliberately sparse, which makes them easy to miss on a short visit.
